,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducable on v4.5.1.stable.official [f62fdbde1]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - macOS Sonoma (14.8.3) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M3 Max (Apple9) - Apple M3 Max (16 threads) - 64.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn the Shader Editor for a VisualShader, if you select all nodes in a frame, including the frame, then duplicate them, the duplicated nodes do not end up in the new frame.  Instead they remain within the original frame.\n\nThere are two workflows here that should be supported:\n* duplicating nodes within the Frame (works right now)\n* duplicating an entire frame, and nodes inside; new nodes should end up in new frame\n\nExample:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3feac2d4-b20d-4ac2-8c9b-8023f8b98045\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n* Create a new VisualShader\n* Add a handful of nodes\n* Add a Frame node\n* Drag nodes into Frame Node\n* Drag to select everything\n* Duplicate\n* Click and drag frame title; all nodes will be in the original frame\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_ur